      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2004 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Encouraging results have been obtained with drug-eluting stents (DESs) to prevent restenosis following PCI. However, DESs are not immune from restenosis and we describe a case of \"candy wrapper\" effect, commonly observed with intracoronary brachytherapy (IBT). In this article, we review the common drawbacks of DES and IBT and their prevention."
      },
